msgid "include::partial$wood-elves.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "Woodland Folk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:109
msgid ""
"Due to living amongst the forests of Loren all Wood Elf infantry does not "
"suffer the usual −1 Command penalty when within woodland."
msgstr ""

#
#
#
#. 2: "2" missing
#. 3: Spelling Armour, Spelling Waywatchers, infiltration
#. 6: Spelling its
#. 7: Spelling penalty
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[glade-guard,†1]]1. Glade Guard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:128
msgid ""
"Wood Elves are just as famed for their bow as their High Elf cousins, and as "
"such Glade Guard units add +1 to their dice roll when making shooting "
"attacks. Therefore these units score a hit against targets in the open on a "
"3+, against defended targets on a 4+, and against fortified targets on a 5+."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wardancers,†2]]2. Wardancers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Wardancer stands are not deployed as independent units. Instead, any Glade "
"Guard or Eternal Guard unit may add one stand of Wardancers. This brings the "
"size of the unit to 4 stands – 3 regular stands plus the Wardancers stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:137
msgid ""
"Wardancers always have the same Armour value as the rest of their unit. They "
"fight as part of their unit and can be removed as a unit casualty if the "
"player wishes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:141
msgid ""
"Wardancers casualties never count for Command penalties.  Wardancers stands "
"never cause the parent unit to be in Irregular Formation no matter how they "
"are placed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[waywatchers,†3]]3. Waywatchers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:147
msgid ""
"Famous for their bow skills even by a Wood Elf standards, Waywatchers shoot "
"the enemy with terrifying accuracy. The add +1 to their dice roll when "
"making shooting attacks and these attacks are resolved at −1 Armour value of "
"the enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:170
msgid ""
"Waywatchers can also ambush. Individual units can be infiltrated onto the "
"battlefield once the game has begun. To infiltrate a unit, the Wood Elf "
"player nominates the point where he wants the Waywatchers to appear and "
"issues an ‘infiltration’ order from any character. The character does not "
"have to be within his normal command range to issue an infiltration order – "
"the character’s command range is considered to extend over the entire "
"tabletop when issuing an infiltration order. Treat the order as issued to "
"the nominated point, and apply any modifiers for distance and proximity of "
"enemy, but ignore penalties of dense terrain. The nominated point must lie "
"either on the table within dense terrain or on any base edge other than the "
"enemy player’s own table edge. If successful, place one stand on the "
"nominated spot and arrange the rest of the unit around it. The infiltrated "
"unit cannot be placed so that it touches an enemy unit. Once deployed, "
"orders can be given to the unit by the same character that gave the "
"infiltration order if he is within his normal command range, the "
"infiltrating unit is considered to have used its first order to deploy. If "
"the infiltration order is failed the unit is not deployed and cannot "
"infiltrate that turn, it can attempt to infiltrate in a subsequent turn at "
"the same of a different place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[forest-spirits,†4]]4. Forest Spirits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:174
msgid ""
"Forest Spirits are woodland creatures. They are immune to terror and suffer "
"−1 Command penalty when being ordered by General or Noble."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wild-riders,†5]]5. Wild Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:177
msgid ""
"Wild Riders receive +1 Attack in the first round of every combat when "
"fighting to the front."
msgstr ""
"Les Cavaliers Sauvages reçoivent un bonus de +1 Attaque le premier tour de "
"chaque combat quand ils attaquent de front."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[warhawk-riders,†6]]6. Warhawk Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:184
msgid ""
"Warhawk Riders can fly. They have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° "
"vision – stands in this unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the "
"purpose of evading and shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. "
"Note that this unit still needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge "
"an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Les Guerriers Faucons peuvent voler. Ils ont une portée de tir de 15cm et "
"une vision à 360° - c'est-à-dire que les socles de l'unité peuvent tracer "
"une ligne de vue depuis n'importe quel bord de leur socle, ceci afin "
"d'éviter ou de tirer, incluant le tir sur les ennemis en charge. Notez que "
"l'unité a tout de même besoin d'avoir une Ligne de Vue depuis son bord avant "
"pour charger un ennemi."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:185
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[treeman,†7]]7. Treeman"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:188
msgid ""
"Treeman can enter woods and suffers no command penalty for being within the "
"woods but cannot get defended status there. Treeman causes terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[treeman-ancient,†8]]8. Treeman Ancient"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:195
msgid ""
"Treeman Ancient has −1 Command penalty when issuing orders to other than "
"Forest Spirit units.  Can join only Forest Spirit units and is able to cast "
"Tree Singing spell. Units joined by Treeman Ancient cause terror. There can "
"ever be only one Treeman Ancient in any Wood Elf army.  Cannot be given any "
"magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[branchwraith,†9]]9. Branchwraith"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:200
msgid ""
"Branchwraith has −1 Command penalty when issuing orders to other than Forest "
"Spirit units. Can join only Forest Spirit units and is able to cast Tree "
"Singing spell. Cannot be given any magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-stag,†10]]10. Giant Stag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:203
msgid ""
"General, Nobles and Spell Weavers may ride a Giant Stag. The Stag adds +1 "
"Attack to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[unicorn,†11]]11. Unicorn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:210
msgid ""
"This mount can be ridden by Spell Weaver only.  The Unicorn adds +1 Attack "
"to those of its rider. Once per battle the Unicorn’s magical power adds +1 "
"to the dice when casting a spell. The player must announce that the "
"Unicorn’s magic before rolling to see if the spell works. There can be only "
"one Unicorn in the army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[warhawk,†12]]12. Warhawk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:214
msgid ""
"General, Nobles and Spell Weavers may ride a Warhawk. The Warhawk can fly, "
"increasing its rider’s move from 60cm to 100cm, and it adds +1 Attack to "
"those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:215
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[forest-dragon,†13]]13. Forest Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:217
msgid "Generals, Nobles and Spell Weavers may ride Forest Dragons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wood Elf spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tree Singing"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling their
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:233
msgid ""
"_The Spell Weaver calls force a mass of tangling branches to surround their "
"troops, protecting them form harm._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:239
msgid ""
"This spell may be cast upon a single unengaged friendly Infantry unit within "
"range, regardless of whether the caster can see them or not. The spell lasts "
"until the start of the caster’s next turn, or until the target unit moves in "
"any way. The target Infantry unit counts as Defended, even if it is in open "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twilight Host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:246
msgid "_A weird enchantment forms around the target unit._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:248
msgid "The target unit causes terror until Wood Elf next magic phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call of the Hunt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:257
msgid ""
"_The Spell Weaver’s voice sings out across the battlefield directing troops "
"above the tumult of combat with the magical Call of the Hunt._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:261
msgid ""
"Unit may make a charge move into contact with the nearest visible enemy unit "
"in the same way as when charging. Enemy may not shoot at chargers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:263
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fury of the Forest"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:270
msgid ""
"_The spell makes three shooting attacks on all enemy units within 10cm of "
"chosen wooded terrain piece. Units get no armour save if within wooded "
"terrain._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:275
msgid ""
"Unengaged units are not driven back by this spell (the assault comes form "
"the ground beneath their feet). Engaged units carry over any hits scored "
"into the first round of combat; any hits scored count as having been struck "
"in the combat itself."
msgstr ""
